Issue #1696 chat-container half, captured 2026-09-02T16:17:12Z

The patch is applied to /app/backend/open_webui/retrieval/utils.py INSIDE the
pinned image (ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.10.2@sha256:9fcea9c6...), not to
the vendored copy, because the chat image takes its backend from that image.
The function under test is then imported and called for real; only Open WebUI's
own OAuth session resolver and the upstream endpoint are stood in for.

marker count in the patched module:
1

--- call 1: a signed-in user ---

Authorization         : Bearer hk_REDACTED_PROOF_FIXTURE
X-Hive-Upstream-Auth  : Bearer SEARCHING-USER-ACCESS-TOKEN
--- call 2: a user with no resolvable session ---
refused: hive (#1696): no signed-in user credential for this embedding call
request reached the upstream: False
ERROR [open_webui.utils.hive_embed_attribution] hive (#1696): no upstream credential for user user-no-session, refusing to embed under the shared shim key; this spend would otherwise land on a platform account instead of on the customer

Reading: the shim key stays on Authorization, which is what gates the carrier
at edge-api, and the searching user's own token rides on X-Hive-Upstream-Auth.
A user with no resolvable session is refused before the request is made, so
nothing goes out under the shared key.
